WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
To make a charged particle faster,
push it with an electric field.

2
00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:06.560
The field does work on it.

3
00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:09.320
To steer it, use a magnetic field.

4
00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:12.720
The force is sideways, so
the speed stays the same.

5
00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:14.870
Only the direction changes.

6
00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.530
Keep steering, and the
path closes into a circle.

7
00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:21.850
So why aren't the most
powerful machines compact?

8
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.330
Why build them as enormous rings?

9
00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.320
In this mission, you'll
take a synchrotron apart:

10
00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:32.670
bending magnets, focusing magnets, and
cavities that add energy every lap.

11
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.930
Then you'll send two beams
round in opposite directions,

12
00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.050
and make them collide head-on.

13
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.880
Your mission: explain why the most powerful
accelerators have to be built as such

14
00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:44.200
huge rings.
